# Product Requirements Document (PRD)

## Project Name

**Distributed Web-Based Real-Time Chat Application**

**Version:** 1.0
**Author:** Ravikishan Singh

---

# 1. Product Overview

The Distributed Web-Based Real-Time Chat Application is a scalable messaging platform that enables users to communicate instantly through private and group conversations. The system uses a distributed architecture with multiple backend servers, Redis Pub/Sub for message synchronization, MongoDB for data storage, and Socket.IO for real-time communication. The application is designed to be secure, highly available, and capable of handling increasing user traffic through horizontal scaling.

---

# 2. Problem Statement

Most traditional chat applications built on a single server face performance bottlenecks, downtime, and scalability limitations as the number of users increases. The goal of this project is to build a distributed chat application that ensures low-latency communication, high availability, fault tolerance, and seamless scalability while providing a smooth user experience.

---

# 3. Goals

* Build a scalable distributed chat platform.
* Enable real-time messaging with minimal latency.
* Support private and group chats.
* Provide secure authentication and authorization.
* Ensure reliable message delivery.
* Design a cloud-ready architecture using Docker.

---

# 4. Target Users

* Students
* Developers
* Small and medium businesses
* Remote teams
* Organizations requiring secure internal communication

---

# 5. Core Features

* User Registration & Login
* JWT Authentication
* User Profile Management
* One-to-One Chat
* Group Chat
* Real-Time Messaging
* Typing Indicators
* Online/Offline Presence
* Read Receipts
* Message Reactions
* File & Image Sharing
* Notifications
* Search Users
* Admin Dashboard
* Secure Logout

---

# 6. Functional Requirements

* Users can create and manage accounts.
* Users can send and receive messages instantly.
* Users can create and manage groups.
* Messages are stored permanently in MongoDB.
* Redis synchronizes messages across backend servers.
* Users receive real-time notifications.
* Files and images can be uploaded and shared securely.
* Admins can manage users and monitor the system.

---

# 7. Non-Functional Requirements

* Response time below 300 ms.
* High availability and fault tolerance.
* Horizontal scalability.
* Secure communication using HTTPS.
* JWT-based authentication.
* Responsive UI.
* Cross-browser compatibility.
* Docker-based deployment.

---

# 8. Technology Stack

| Layer            | Technology                         |
| ---------------- | ---------------------------------- |
| Frontend         | React.js, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS |
| Backend          | Node.js, Express.js                |
| Real-Time        | Socket.IO                          |
| Database         | MongoDB                            |
| Message Broker   | Redis Pub/Sub                      |
| Authentication   | JWT, bcrypt                        |
| File Storage     | Cloudinary                         |
| Reverse Proxy    | Nginx                              |
| Containerization | Docker & Docker Compose            |
| Monitoring       | Prometheus & Grafana               |

---

# 9. MVP (Minimum Viable Product)

The first version of the application will include:

* User authentication
* Private chat
* Group chat
* Real-time messaging
* File sharing
* Online presence
* Notifications
* Responsive web interface

---

# 10. Success Metrics

* Message delivery latency below 200 ms.
* API response time below 300 ms.
* 99%+ successful message delivery.
* Support for multiple backend servers.
* High user satisfaction and reliable uptime.

---

# 11. Risks

* Redis server failure affecting synchronization.
* Network interruptions causing temporary disconnections.
* Large file uploads increasing storage usage.
* Security vulnerabilities if authentication is misconfigured.
* High concurrent traffic impacting performance.

---

